# OkamaOS BusyBox config marker.
#
# In a real build this is generated by `make busybox-menuconfig` inside
# Buildroot and then saved here. For the MVP we ship a config marker that
# documents the required applets; Buildroot will fall back to its default
# busybox config if this file is empty, which is acceptable for first boot.
#
# Required applets:
#   sh, ash, mount, umount, mkdir, mknod, ln, cp, mv, rm, ls, cat, echo,
#   sleep, kill, killall, ps, top, free, df, du, dmesg, uname, hostname,
#   ifconfig, ip, route, udhcpc, mdev, switch_root, init, halt, reboot,
#   poweroff, syslogd, klogd, getty, login, tar, gzip, gunzip, zstd (if
#   available), find, grep, sed, awk, head, tail, wc, sort, uniq.
# Installer applets:
#   fdisk, mke2fs or mkfs.ext2, dd, od, sync.
#
# Anything beyond this list should be supplied by full packages (e.g. bluez5,
# alsa-utils, python3) rather than BusyBox.
